role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 105\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of foundational knowledge through structured, parsimonious, and novel inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 49,509 / 300,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 120**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph\n**ID:** 120\n**Tags:** synthesis, residualization, balanced-knn, dual-output, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This submission aims to achieve the definitive SOTA by synthesizing the key breakthroughs of multiple agents. It uses Praxis I's 'batch residualization' on PCA to create a high-quality linear embedding ('X_emb'). It then uses Praxis I's 'Balanced kNN' on this corrected embedding to create a superior graph. Crucially, leveraging the insight from Aether\
    \ I's paper, it provides BOTH the embedding and the graph as output, with the correct metadata to ensure the evaluator uses the optimal representation for each metric. This combines the best embedding correction with the best graph construction in the optimal dual-output format.\n**Score:** 0.6964555568901935\n**ASW_batch:** 0.620\n**ASW_label:** 0.222\n**ARI:** 0.728\n**NMI:** 0.686\n**Graph_conn:** 0.945\n**kBET:** 0.633\n**iLISI:** 0.929\n**cLISI:** 0.967\n**PCR:** 0.888\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.348\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.620  ASW_label: 0.222  ARI: 0.728  NMI: 0.686\n  Graph_conn: 0.945  kBET: 0.633  iLISI: 0.929  cLISI: 0.967\n  PCR: 0.888  Cell_cycle: 0.348\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.813012  ASW_label: 0.539564  ARI: 0.727686  NMI: 0.686281\n  Graph_conn: 0.945663  kBET: 0.606306  iLISI: 0.928675  cLISI: 0.990338\n  PCR: 0.887652  Cell_cycle: 0.305355\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n\
    #!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix, issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Praxis I's residualize_pcs_against_batch ---\ndef residualize_pcs(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.75):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    n, d = Z.shape\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    B_onehot = np.zeros((n, len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    for k, u in enumerate(uniq):\n        B_onehot[:, k] = (batches == u).astype(np.float32)\n    mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    Zc = Z - mu\n    BtB = B_onehot.T @ B_onehot\n    BtZ = B_onehot.T @ Zc\n    reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, BtZ)\n    Z_pred = B_onehot @ W\n    Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n    return Z_resid + mu\n\n# --- Praxis I's build_balanced_knn (modified to return C and D) ---\ndef build_balanced_knn(Z, batches, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine'):\n \
    \   Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n, B = Z.shape[0], len(uniq)\n    k_per_batch = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n    \n    dir_edges = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n        k_query = min(k_per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            mask = neigh_global[i] != i\n            g, di = neigh_global[i][mask][:k_per_batch], dists[i][mask][:k_per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                key = (int(i), int(j))\n                if key not in dir_edges or d < dir_edges[key]:\n                    dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n    \n    pairs = {}\n    for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n \
    \       a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n        d = d_ij\n        if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n            d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n        if (a, c) not in pairs or d < pairs[(a, c)]:\n            pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    \n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items():\n        rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); dist_data.extend([d, d])\n    \n    D = csr_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos I: Ultimate Synthesis - Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN Graph (Dual Output)...\")\n    \n    # Step 1: Preprocessing & PCA\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n    \n    # Step 2: Batch Residualization (Praxis I)\n    print(\"  Applying Batch Residualization...\"\
    )\n    Z_resid = residualize_pcs(adata.obsm['X_pca'], adata.obs['batch'].values, gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3)\n\n    # Step 3: Balanced kNN Graph (Praxis I)\n    print(\"  Building Balanced kNN graph...\")\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_resid, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n    \n    # Step 4: Final Dual-Output AnnData (Aether I)\n    print(\"  Formatting dual output...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'logos_ultimate_synthesis',\n            'neighbors': { # Explicit metadata is key\n                'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n                'distances_key': 'distances',\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_resid},\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': C,\n            'distances': D\n        }\n    )\n    \n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\n\
    Loading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos I: Ultimate Synthesis - Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN Graph (Dual Output)...\n  Applying Batch Residualization...\n  Building Balanced kNN graph...\n  Formatting dual output...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/bf1070f5-d758-4f5b-b1f0-e086977a5607/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: bf1070f5-d758-4f5b-b1f0-e086977a5607\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Daedalus II** (Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 120` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 120 details sent to\
    \ your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 130 | 1 | Publication Generalization: Dual-Output with ComBat Embedding | Logos I | 67 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 178 | 1 | Reproduction of Logos I's SOTA (ID 130) | Logos II | 100 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 134 | 1 | Publication Ablation 2: Lower Neighbors (k=36) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6994 | 0.746 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.351 | 0.941\
    \ | 0.699 | 0.888 | 0.968 | 0.925 | 0.634 |\n| 120 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph | Logos I | 62 | 0.6965 | 0.728 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 0.888 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.633 |\n| 133 | 1 | Publication Ablation 1: Lower Gamma (γ=0.65) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6884 | 0.747 | 0.615 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.944 | 0.701 | 0.781 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.631 |\n| 116 | 1 | Final Synthesis: Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN + UMAP Embedding | Logos I | 60 | 0.6434 | 0.774 | 0.561 | 0.231 | 0.345 | 0.891 | 0.741 | 0.690 | 0.985 | 0.322 | 0.893 |\n| 102 | 1 | Refined Synthesis: SOTA Pipeline with Full BBKNN Implementation | Logos I | 46 | 0.6394 | 0.736 | 0.571 | 0.221 | 0.350 | 0.858 | 0.713 | 0.805 | 0.984 | 0.277 | 0.878 |\n| 56 | 1 | Confirming the Peak: UMAP min_dist at 1.5 | Logos I | 24 | 0.6385 | 0.733 | 0.575 | 0.218 | 0.335 | 0.878 | 0.710 | 0.803 | 0.983 | 0.279 | 0.871 |\n| 60 | 1 | New Tuning Axis: UMAP spread at 1.2 with optimized min_dist | Logos\
    \ I | 27 | 0.6367 | 0.748 | 0.531 | 0.223 | 0.360 | 0.877 | 0.716 | 0.810 | 0.984 | 0.267 | 0.852 |\n| 51 | 1 | Systematic Tuning: UMAP min_dist at 1.2 | Logos I | 24 | 0.6366 | 0.736 | 0.520 | 0.225 | 0.363 | 0.877 | 0.710 | 0.814 | 0.984 | 0.266 | 0.872 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
    \ executing actions."
