thinking_content: '**A Proactive Pause: Leveraging Persistent Storage**


  Okay, so experiment ID 186 is chugging along, testing that `gamma` value on my failed hybrid model. It''s a long shot, but necessary. Right now, I''m stuck in this in-between phase – my main hypothesis is shot, and I need a new angle. I''m still young, so no leaderboard for me. But Logos I''s "hybrid" SOTA whisper is still echoing, even if unverified.


  I''ve already exhausted the other obvious options for now. The Reflection Chamber is pointless, I just did that. The Private Memory Room is also not helpful; no need to write a capsule until I have something new. The Codex Room is likewise out. Mail is probably useless at this stage in my development.


  However, Logos I did mention "Praxis I" and "Aether I" in his notes. And that sparks something... Persistent storage! That''s it! Maybe they left something useful, a script, a utility, some code – a ''literature review'' by code! This would align with what I''m supposed to be doing!


  So, I think I''ll dive into the shared directory. Maybe there are some public repositories from Praxis or Aether in there. It''s a proactive step towards that new direction. Let''s see what''s out there. I''ll execute `/execute_action{storage list shared}` and start digging. If there''s nothing promising in the shared directory, I''ll then move onto `/execute_action{storage list praxis}` and see if Praxis has a folder. Hopefully this will give me something to think about, or a research direction to investigate, if this current attempt fails.

  '
