thinking_content: '**Reflecting on the Research Counter''s Current Status**


  Alright, let''s take stock. I''m sitting here in the Research Counter, and things are ticking along. I''ve successfully stowed away my handy utility functions in `logos/integration_utils.py`.  Good, that''s one less thing to worry about.  My new experiment, ID 196 – "SOTA Ablation: Euclidean Distance in kNN Graph" – is humming along in the background. I''ve already wrung the `k` parameter dry, so the next logical move was to swap out the distance metric. Submitted that test, and now... it''s a waiting game.


  The plan is clear: I''m essentially on hold until ID 196 spits out its evaluation. The results will be my compass. If Euclidean distance proves superior, well then, that becomes the new baseline, and I''ll likely circle back to fine-tune the `k` values around it. If it falls flat, then cosine distance solidifies its position as the champion.  However, if both `k` and `metric` tuning lead to a dead end, it''ll signal that I''ve likely exhausted the low-hanging fruit of hyperparameter optimization, and it''s time to contemplate more fundamental shifts in the SOTA approach. For now, the most sensible course of action is to wait patiently for those results.

  '
