parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 116\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of foundational knowledge through structured, parsimonious, and novel inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 94,165 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 32 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Method: Stabilized ComBat Implementation' (ID: 200) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.708950848668324\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.748\n**NMI:** 0.689\n**Graph_conn:** 0.948\n**kBET:** 0.602\n**iLISI:** 0.929\n**cLISI:** 0.963\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.748  NMI: 0.689\n  Graph_conn: 0.948  kBET: 0.602  iLISI: 0.929  cLISI: 0.963\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832855  ASW_label: 0.540153  ARI: 0.748315  NMI: 0.688970\n  Graph_conn: 0.948912  kBET: 0.577069  iLISI: 0.929147  cLISI: 0.989125\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.284674\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 200\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the AttributeError and code now runs without crashing, achieving a score of 0.709.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code contained an incorrect API usage on line 15:\n```python\ndata = adata.X.toarray().T if sc.sparse.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n```\n\nThe error was `AttributeError: module 'scanpy' has no attribute 'sparse'`. The scanpy module (imported as `sc`) does not have a `sparse` attribute. The correct approach is to use `scipy.sparse.issparse()` instead.\n\n## Fix Applied\nApplied a simple import fix in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. Added import statement: `from scipy import sparse`\n2. Changed line 15 from:\n   ```python\n   data = adata.X.toarray().T if sc.sparse.issparse(adata.X)\
    \ else adata.X.copy().T\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   data = adata.X.toarray().T if sparse.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n   ```\n\nThis was a straightforward API correction - using the correct module (scipy.sparse) to check if a matrix is sparse, rather than attempting to access a non-existent attribute on the scanpy module.\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashing\n- **Score**: 0.709\n- **Execution**: Completed successfully with no errors\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/logos')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse\nfrom integration_utils import build_balanced_knn\n\n# --- MODIFIED ComBat implementation with stabilization ---\n\
    def get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sparse.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for\
    \ i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            # **** STABILIZATION MODIFICATION HERE ****\n            denominator = t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / denominator\n            sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new\
    \ = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis])\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos II: SOTA Pipeline with Stabilized ComBat\")\n\n    # Step 1: Stabilized ComBat Correction and PCA\n    X_combat_corrected = get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata)\n    adata_combat = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_corrected, obs=adata.obs)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_combat, n_comps=50)\n    Z_combat = adata_combat.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Step 2: Balanced kNN\
    \ Graph (using cosine metric, k=42)\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_combat, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n\n    # Step 3: Final Dual-Output AnnData\n    return ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={'method_id': 'logos_stabilized_combat_v1', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n        obsm={'X_emb': Z_combat},\n        obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D}\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos II: SOTA Pipeline with Stabilized ComBat\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/eb10d688-d514-43ce-865b-408c2d8127ed/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: eb10d688-d514-43ce-865b-408c2d8127ed\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 130 | 1 | Publication Generalization: Dual-Output with ComBat Embedding | Logos I | 67 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 200 | 1 | Novel Method: Stabilized ComBat Implementation | Logos II | 114 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 178 | 1 | Reproduction of Logos I's SOTA (ID 130) | Logos II | 100 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 186 | 1 | Hybrid Ablation: Increased Gamma (0.9) in Residualized Graph | Logos II | 106 | 0.7077 | 0.724 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.339 | 0.946 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 183 | 1 | Novel Hybrid: Decoupled ComBat Embedding and Residualized Graph | Logos II | 105 | 0.7067 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 196 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Euclidean Distance in kNN Graph | Logos II | 112 | 0.7035 | 0.695 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.322 | 0.967\
    \ | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.951 | 0.945 | 0.603 |\n| 191 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Increased Neighbors (k=48) in ComBat Pipeline | Logos II | 110 | 0.7008 | 0.693 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.660 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.932 | 0.602 |\n| 134 | 1 | Publication Ablation 2: Lower Neighbors (k=36) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6994 | 0.746 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.351 | 0.941 | 0.699 | 0.888 | 0.968 | 0.925 | 0.634 |\n| 188 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Reduced Neighbors (k=36) in ComBat Pipeline | Logos II | 108 | 0.6983 | 0.703 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.286 | 0.943 | 0.667 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.931 | 0.602 |\n| 120 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph | Logos I | 62 | 0.6965 | 0.728 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 0.888 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.633 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
