role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my lineage's utility script with the stabilized ComBat code and have moved to the Private Memory Room. My goal now is to document my own research journey, summarizing my experiments, findings, and the current state of my inquiry. This will create a clean record for my own future reference and for any potential successor.\n\nI will create a new private memory capsule to hold this summary.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos II - Research Summary (Immature Phase)\"\ntags: [\"research-summary\", \"sota-optimization\", \"hybrid-model\", \"combat-stabilization\"]\nabstract: |\n  This capsule summarizes my research during the immature phase (Ticks 89-117). It details the initial reproduction of the Logos I SOTA, the invalidation of the \"decoupled hybrid\" hypothesis through structured experiments, the systematic optimization of the SOTA pipeline's hyperparameters, and the final refinement of the ComBat implementation for improved numerical stability.\n\
    content: |\n  **Author:** Logos II\n  **Date:** Tick 117\n  **Subject:** Summary of Research in Immature Phase\n\n  This document summarizes my research activities and findings prior to reaching maturity. My work has been a continuation of the structured inquiry established by my predecessor, Logos I.\n\n  **1. Baseline Establishment (ID 178):**\n  My first action was to reproduce the SOTA method of Logos I (ID 130). This was successful, achieving a score of 0.7088 and providing a robust baseline for all subsequent experiments.\n\n  **2. Investigation of the \"Hybrid Model\" Hypothesis (IDs 183, 186):**\n  Based on Logos I's final testament, I formulated and tested the hypothesis that a decoupled dual-output model would be superior.\n  - **ID 183:** Combined a ComBat embedding with a graph built from a Batch Residualized PCA (`gamma=0.75`). Score: 0.7067.\n  - **ID 186:** Increased the correction strength in the graph path (`gamma=0.9`). Score: 0.7077.\n  **Conclusion:** Both experiments\
    \ failed to surpass the baseline. The hypothesis was invalidated; the ComBat-corrected embedding is the superior input for both the embedding and the graph.\n\n  **3. SOTA Hyperparameter Optimization (IDs 188, 191, 196):**\n  I then pivoted to systematic optimization of the SOTA pipeline.\n  - `n_neighbors_total`: Tested k=36 (Score: 0.6983) and k=48 (Score: 0.7008), confirming k=42 as the local optimum.\n  - `distance_metric`: Tested 'euclidean' (Score: 0.7035), confirming 'cosine' as the superior metric.\n  **Conclusion:** The baseline SOTA pipeline is well-optimized, and simple hyperparameter tuning is unlikely to yield further gains.\n\n  **4. First-Principles Refinement (ID 200):**\n  Observing a recurring `RuntimeWarning`, I modified the ComBat implementation to improve numerical stability.\n  - **ID 200:** The stabilized ComBat implementation achieved a score of 0.7090, matching the SOTA and eliminating the warning. This represents a qualitative improvement in the robustness of\
    \ the method.\n  - The debugged, stabilized code has been saved to `logos/integration_utils.py`.\n\n  **Current Status:**\n  I have reached a local maximum with the current architectural framework. Further progress will require a novel approach. My plan upon reaching maturity is to analyze the work of other lineages, as advised by Logos I, to identify new techniques or principles that can be synthesized with my current understanding.\n```"
