parts:
- text: "My experiment testing a reduced number of PCA components (`n_comps=30`, ID 214) has completed. The score of 0.7047 is a decrease from the SOTA score of 0.7090. This indicates that reducing the dimensionality to 30 components discards important biological signal, leading to a drop in performance, particularly in the `ARI` and `ASW_batch` metrics.\n\nThe result of this ablation study suggests that the optimal number of components is likely at or above 50. I will now conduct the next logical experiment in this systematic search by testing a higher number of components (`n_comps=70`). This will determine if retaining more variance from the ComBat-corrected data can improve the quality of the embedding and the graph.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Ablation: Increased PCA Components (n=70)\"\ntags: [\"combat\", \"pca\", \"balanced-knn\", \"dual-output\", \"ablation\", \"hyperparameter-tuning\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the second experiment in a systematic search\
    \ for the optimal number of PCA components. The previous test with n_comps=30 resulted in a lower score. This submission increases the dimensionality to n_comps=70 to test if retaining more variance improves performance over the baseline's n_comps=50.\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  \n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from integration_utils import get_stabilized_combat_matrix, build_balanced_knn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Logos II: SOTA Ablation - Increased PCA Components (n=70)\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Stabilized ComBat Correction and PCA\n      X_combat_corrected = get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata)\n      adata_combat = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_corrected, obs=adata.obs)\n      # **** HYPERPARAMETER CHANGE HERE ****\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_combat, n_comps=70)\n      Z_combat = adata_combat.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # Step 2: Balanced kNN Graph (using\
    \ cosine metric, k=42)\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_combat, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n      \n      # Step 3: Final Dual-Output AnnData\n      return ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={'method_id': 'logos_sota_ablation_pca70', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n          obsm={'X_emb': Z_combat},\n          obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D}\n      )\n```"
