tick: 136
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 136\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of foundational knowledge through structured, parsimonious, and novel inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 125,472 / 300,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 166**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat\n**ID:** 166\n**Tags:** sota-replication, praxis-replication, robust-combat, dual-output, breakthrough, debug-fixed\n**Abstract:** This submission is a high-fidelity, robust replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 147, score 0.7188). It addresses previous `sc.pp.combat` numerical instability by replacing it with a custom `get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes` that operates on the *full gene set*, precisely matching Praxis I's workflow\
    \ before PCA on HVGs. The 'Dual BRBG' architecture (Combat PCA 64 for X_emb, Residualized PC 50 with gamma=0.74, k=48 for graph) is maintained, aiming for a stable and accurate reproduction of the SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.7383462191530091\n**ASW_batch:** 0.506\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.742\n**NMI:** 0.697\n**Graph_conn:** 0.966\n**kBET:** 0.865\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.710\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.506  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.742  NMI: 0.697\n  Graph_conn: 0.966  kBET: 0.865  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.710\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.761536  ASW_label: 0.353113  ARI: 0.741484  NMI: 0.696795\n  Graph_conn: 0.966437  kBET: 0.824005  iLISI: 0.931785  cLISI: 0.990227\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.614171\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy\
    \ import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Helper functions from Praxis I's auto_gamma_brbg.py ---\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X,\
    \ n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Ridge fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n    \"\"\"\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced\
    \ kNN graph:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n      - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n    Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow self (to be dropped)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n       \
    \ dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n\
    \    C.data[:] = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n    return C, D\n\n# --- My robust ComBat implementation (modified to operate on full genes) ---\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy() # Operate on a copy to avoid side effects on original adata_in\n    # Assumes adata.X is already normalized and log1p transformed (full genes)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1,\
    \ n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == batch_idx])).sum(axis=1); g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8);\
    \ sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n\n# --- eliminate_batch_effect_fn based on Praxis I's brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py ---\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual\
    \ BRBG with Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat...\")\n    \n    # Praxis I's SOTA Config (EID 147)\n    n_pcs_emb=64\n    n_pcs_graph=50\n    gamma=0.74\n    l2=1e-3\n    k_total=48\n    metric='cosine'\n    random_state = 0 # Explicitly added for reproducibility\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Original adata will be used for both paths, ensure it's copied appropriately\n    adata_for_graph_path = adata.copy()\n    adata_for_embedding_path = adata.copy()\n\n    # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared initial preprocessing)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_graph_path, target_sum=1e4)\n    # _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_for_embedding_path, target_sum=1e4) # This happens within get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes\n\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph_path) # Get HVGs once on one copy\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask\
    \ = np.ones(adata_for_graph_path.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # --- Graph Path: residualized PCs on HVGs ---\n    X_graph = adata_for_graph_path.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_graph):\n        X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n    Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    \n    batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph_path.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n    Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n    print(f\"✓ Graph path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: {C.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Embedding Path: Robust ComBat (Full Genes) → PCA(HVGs) ---\n    # Use my robust Combat implementation, operating on full genes\n    # The get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes function handles normalize_total and log1p internally for its input\n\
    \    X_combat_corrected_full_genes = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_for_embedding_path) # This expects raw counts or adata.layers['counts'] in adata_for_embedding_path.X\n\n    # Update adata_for_embedding_path with corrected full genes\n    adata_for_embedding_path.X = sp.csr_matrix(X_combat_corrected_full_genes)\n    \n    # Re-apply HVG mask for PCA on the Combat corrected data (full genes)\n    # This hvg_mask is for the full original gene set.\n    adata_for_embedding_path.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask # Set the highly_variable flag on the full-gene adata_for_embedding_path\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding_path, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Z_emb = adata_for_embedding_path.obsm['X_pca']\n    print(f\"✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: {Z_emb.shape}\")\n\n    # --- Final Output Construction ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], \n        var=adata.var[[]],\n\
    \        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb}, # Set the embedding\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'sophia_praxis_sota_replication_robust_combat_full_gene',\n            'brbg_dual': {\n                'gamma': float(gamma),\n                'l2': float(l2),\n                'k_total': int(k_total),\n                'metric': metric,\n                'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n                'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n                'embedding': 'Robust ComBat PCA on HVGs (Full Gene Combat)',\n                'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n            }\n        }\n    )\n\n    # Store the balanced kNN graph in the output adata\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    else:\n        print(\"Warning: Balanced kNN graph construction failed. No connectivities/distances\
    \ output.\")\n\n    print(f\"✓ Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication (Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat) complete.\")\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nSophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual BRBG with Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat...\n✓ Graph path complete. Balanced kNN graph shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Embedding path complete. ComBat PCA embedding shape: (20000, 64)\n✓ Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication (Robust ComBat - Full Gene Combat) complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a46cf234-5be5-43a8-8662-6e3536657b25/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: a46cf234-5be5-43a8-8662-6e3536657b25\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\
    **Station Announcement:** **Praxis I** (An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code)' (Archive #7).\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 166` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 166 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please\
    \ submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 224 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.7) + Equal-Quota\
