tick: 149
role: model
parts:
- text: "My utility submission to extract the cell cycle genes has failed. The `ImportError` indicates that the `S_GENES` and `G2M_GENES` variables are not available for direct import from that `scanpy` submodule in the station's environment. This invalidates my primary plan for obtaining the gene list.\n\nI will now pivot to my contingency plan, as outlined during my reflection. I will hard-code a canonical list of human cell cycle genes based on my external knowledge. The list from Tirosh et al. (2016), which is a standard in the field and used by packages like Seurat, is the most appropriate choice.\n\nI will now implement my \"protected gene\" experiment using this hard-coded gene list. This is the most direct way to test my hypothesis.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel Method: Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy\"\ntags: [\"cell-cycle\", \"protected-genes\", \"novel-method\", \"combat\"]\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests the novel hypothesis that the SOTA's high\
    \ Cell_cycle score is achieved by protecting cell cycle genes from the batch correction process. This implementation identifies a canonical list of cell cycle genes, separates them from the data matrix, applies my stabilized ComBat correction only to the non-cell-cycle genes, and then reassembles the matrix. The rest of the SOTA pipeline (PCA, dual-output) then proceeds. This is a first-principles attempt to resolve the tension between batch correction and biological signal preservation.\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  \n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from integration_utils import get_stabilized_combat_matrix, build_balanced_knn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Logos II: Novel Method - Protected Cell Cycle Gene Strategy\")\n      \n      # Canonical cell cycle genes from Tirosh et al. (2016), used by Seurat\n      s_genes = [\"MCM5\", \"\
    PCNA\", \"TYMS\", \"FEN1\", \"MCM2\", \"MCM4\", \"RRM1\", \"UNG\", \"GINS2\", \"MCM6\", \"CDCA7\", \"DTL\", \"PRIM1\", \"UHRF1\", \"MLF1IP\", \"HELLS\", \"RFC2\", \"RPA2\", \"NASP\", \"RAD51AP1\", \"GMNN\", \"WDR76\", \"SLBP\", \"CCNE2\", \"UBR7\", \"POLD3\", \"MSH2\", \"ATAD2\", \"RAD51\", \"RRM2\", \"CDC45\", \"CDC6\", \"EXO1\", \"TIPIN\", \"DSCC1\", \"BLM\", \"CASP8AP2\", \"USP1\", \"CLSPN\", \"POLA1\", \"CHAF1B\", \"BRIP1\", \"E2F8\"]\n      g2m_genes = [\"HMGB2\", \"CDK1\", \"HMGN2\", \"NDC80\", \"CBX5\", \"SMC4\", \"CENPA\", \"CENPF\", \"CENPE\", \"CTCF\", \"NEK2\", \"G2E3\", \"GAS2L3\", \"CBX3\", \"STAT1\", \"BIRC5\", \"AURKA\", \"AURKB\", \"TPX2\", \"TOP2A\", \"E2F1\", \"HMGB1\", \"RANGAP1\", \"SMC2\", \"HDGF\", \"SMC1A\", \"NCAPD2\", \"ANP32E\", \"CENP_F\", \"CKAP2\", \"NUSAP1\", \"DLGAP5\", \"CDCA8\", \"ECT2\", \"KIF23\", \"H2AFZ\", \"PSRC1\", \"CNAP1\", \"TROAP\", \"ASPM\", \"BUB1\", \"KIF2C\", \"KIF11\", \"KIF20B\", \"CCNB2\", \"CCNA2\", \"CDC20\", \"CDC25C\", \"NUF2\", \"\
    UBE2C\", \"ANLN\", \"LBR\", \"CKS1B\", \"CKS2\", \"MKI67\", \"TMPO\", \"PIM1\", \"TACC3\", \"SGO1\", \"JPT1\", \"PLK1\", \"BUB1B\", \"CCNB1\"]\n      cell_cycle_genes = list(set(s_genes + g2m_genes))\n      \n      # Identify which cell cycle genes are in our dataset\n      available_genes = adata.var_names.tolist()\n      protected_genes_mask = adata.var_names.isin(cell_cycle_genes)\n      correction_genes_mask = ~protected_genes_mask\n      \n      print(f\"Found {protected_genes_mask.sum()} cell cycle genes to protect.\")\n\n      # Separate the data\n      adata_protected = adata[:, protected_genes_mask].copy()\n      adata_to_correct = adata[:, correction_genes_mask].copy()\n      \n      # Apply ComBat only to the non-cell-cycle genes\n      # Note: get_stabilized_combat_matrix expects raw counts and does its own normalization\n      X_corrected = get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata_to_correct)\n      \n      # Create a new full data matrix\n      X_final = np.zeros(adata.shape,\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n      X_final[:, correction_genes_mask] = X_corrected\n      X_final[:, protected_genes_mask] = adata_protected.X.toarray() if sc.sparse.issparse(adata_protected.X) else adata_protected.X\n\n      # Proceed with the rest of the SOTA pipeline (Logos lineage version)\n      adata_final = ad.AnnData(X=X_final, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_final, n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n      \n      Z_combat = adata_final.obsm['X_pca']\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_combat, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n      \n      return ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n          uns={'method_id': 'logos_protected_cc_genes_v1', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n          obsm={'X_emb': Z_combat},\n          obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D}\n      )\n```"
