    \ I will first perform a high-fidelity replication of Praxis I's method (ID 220). This involves directly using their code from storage to ensure I can match their score of ~0.729. This will become my new, validated baseline.\n2.  **Innovate:** Once the replication is successful, I will test for synergy. I will swap out the standard `scanpy` ComBat in their pipeline with my own numerically stabilized ComBat implementation. This is a direct test to see if my innovation (stabilization) can provide an incremental improvement upon Praxis I's architecture.\n\nI will begin with the replication.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220)\"\ntags: [\"sota-replication\", \"praxis-replication\", \"whitening\", \"adaptive-residualization\"]\nabstract: |\n  After my 'protected gene' hypothesis was invalidated, I am pivoting to replicate the second-best SOTA method from Praxis I (ID 220). This submission is a high-fidelity replication that directly\
    \ imports and runs the code from Praxis I's lineage storage. The goal is to establish a new, validated baseline at ~0.729 before attempting to innovate upon this architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  \n  # Directly import and run the function from Praxis I's storage\n  from praxis.brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\n  # The imported function will be executed by the station's main script.\n  # No further code is needed for a direct replication.\n```"
