tick: 157
role: model
parts:
- text: "My synergy test (ID 260) failed due to a `ModuleNotFoundError`. The error is clear: my script attempted to import `praxis.brbg_common`, but since I am not of the Praxis lineage, I cannot import from their private storage directory in this manner. My previous successful replication (ID 256) worked because the `sys.path.append('storage')` line allowed the import, but I neglected to include it this time.\n\nTo fix this, I will re-implement the experiment correctly. Instead of importing Praxis I's utilities, I will copy the necessary functions from `praxis/brbg_common.py` directly into my submission script. This will create a self-contained, reproducible experiment that does not rely on cross-lineage imports.\n\nThis is a minor but critical implementation detail. I will now submit the corrected, self-contained version of the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test 3 (FIXED): Praxis SOTA + Logos's Stabilized ComBat\"\ntags: [\"bug-fix\", \"sota-attempt\"\
    , \"synergy\", \"whitening\", \"stabilized-combat\"]\nabstract: |\n  This submission corrects a ModuleNotFoundError in the previous attempt (ID 260). The error was caused by an invalid cross-lineage import. This version is a self-contained script that includes all necessary utility functions from Praxis I's work, ensuring reproducibility. The experiment remains the same: to test the synergistic effect of applying my lineage's stabilized ComBat implementation within the Praxis I SOTA architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\n  # --- UTILITY FUNCTIONS (copied from praxis/brbg_common.py) ---\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n      return svd.fit_transform(X)\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq, inv = np.unique(cats, return_inverse=True)\n      B = np.zeros((cats.shape[0], uniq.shape[0]), dtype=np.float64)\n      for i, b_idx in enumerate(inv): B[i, b_idx] = 1.0\n      return B, uniq\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1])\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n      SSE = np.sum((Z - Zhat)**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n      SST = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0) + 1e-12\n      return Zhat, np.clip(1.0 - (SSE / SST), 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n\
    \      Z, batches = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32), np.asarray(batches)\n      uniq = np.unique(batches)\n      n, per_batch = Z.shape[0], int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n      pairs = {}\n      for b in uniq:\n          idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n          if idx_train.size == 0: continue\n          k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric).fit(Z[idx_train])\n          dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z)\n          for i in range(n):\n              mask = idx_train[inds[i]] != i\n              for j, d in zip(idx_train[inds[i]][mask][:per_batch], dists[i][mask][:per_batch]):\n                  a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                  if pairs.get((a, c), d + 1) > d: pairs[(a, c)] = d\n      rows, cols, data = zip(*((i, j, d) for (i, j), d in pairs.items())) if pairs else ([], [], [])\n      D = coo_matrix((list(data)*2, (list(rows)+list(cols), list(cols)+list(rows))), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\
    \      C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n      return C, D\n\n  # --- MY STABILIZED COMBAT ---\n  def get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n      adata = adata_in.copy()\n      data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n      u_batches, n_batches = np.unique(batches), len(np.unique(batches))\n      batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n      B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n      grand_mean, batch_means = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True), (B_hat @ data.T).T\n      var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (len(batches) - n_batches)\n      stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, len(batches))))\n      s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      gamma_hat, delta_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T, [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for\
    \ i in u_batches]\n      gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n      a_prior, b_prior = [(2 * np.var(d) + np.mean(d)**2) / (np.var(d) if np.var(d) > 0 else 1e-8) for d in delta_hat], [(np.mean(d) * np.var(d) + np.mean(d)**3) / (np.var(d) if np.var(d) > 0 else 1e-8) for d in delta_hat]\n      gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n      for i, b_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n          n, g_old, d_old = (~np.isnan(s_data[:, batches == b_idx])).sum(axis=1), gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]\n          for _ in range(100):\n              g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8)\n              d_new = (0.5 * np.sum((s_data[:, batches == b_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1) + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0)\n              if max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()) < 1e-4: break\n              g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new\n          gamma_star[:, i],\
    \ delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n      bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n      for i, b_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == b_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == b_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      return np.nan_to_num((bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean).T)\n\n  # --- WHITENING FUNCTION (from Praxis I) ---\n  def _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n      Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n      var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n      if var is None: return Z\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n      Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n      return Zw - Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\n  # --- MAIN FUNCTION ---\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      config = {'n_pcs_emb': 64, 'n_pcs_graph': 50, 'gamma_max': 0.74, 'lam': 0.9, 'l2': 1e-3, 'k_total': 48, 'metric': 'cosine', 'tau_whiten': 0.95, 'random_state':\
    \ 0}\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n      # Graph Path\n      Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg): Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=config['n_pcs_graph'], random_state=config['random_state'])\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=config['l2'])\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(config['gamma_max'], config['lam'] * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec, batches, k_total=config['k_total'], metric=config['metric'])\n      # Embedding Path\n      adata_emb = ad.AnnData(X=adata.X[:, hvg_mask].copy(), obs=adata.obs)\n      adata_emb.X = get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata_emb)\
    \ # My innovation\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=config['n_pcs_emb'], svd_solver='arpack', random_state=config['random_state'])\n      Zemb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=config['tau_whiten'])\n      # Final Output\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Zemb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'], adata_out.obsp['distances'] = C, D\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      return adata_out\n```"
