parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 162\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of foundational knowledge through structured, parsimonious, and novel inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 217,007 / 300,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 78 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Method: Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1' (ID: 272) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.37184058612742477\n**ASW_batch:** 0.049\n**ASW_label:** 0.023\n**ARI:** 0.216\n**NMI:** 0.324\n**Graph_conn:** 0.505\n**kBET:** 0.137\n**iLISI:** 1.000\n**cLISI:** 0.290\n**PCR:** 0.392\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.782\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.049  ASW_label: 0.023  ARI: 0.216  NMI:\
    \ 0.324\n  Graph_conn: 0.505  kBET: 0.137  iLISI: 1.000  cLISI: 0.290\n  PCR: 0.392  Cell_cycle: 0.782\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.555575  ASW_label: 0.424746  ARI: 0.215796  NMI: 0.324547\n  Graph_conn: 0.513364  kBET: 0.140563  iLISI: 1.000000  cLISI: 0.793225\n  PCR: 0.391816  Cell_cycle: 0.675050\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 272\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the AttributeError in submission v2. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (v1) attempted to check if a matrix is sparse using `sc.sparse.issparse()`, but scanpy doesn't have a `sparse` attribute. The correct approach is to use `scipy.sparse.issparse()` from scipy.\n\n**Error location:** Line 15 of original submission\n```python\nX_orig_normalized = adata_orig.X.toarray() if sc.sparse.issparse(adata_orig.X) else adata_orig.X\n```\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nAttributeError: module 'scanpy' has no attribute 'sparse'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\
    Created `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Added scipy import:** Added `from scipy import sparse` at the top of the file\n2. **Fixed sparse check:** Changed `sc.sparse.issparse()` to `sparse.issparse()`\n\n**Fixed line:**\n```python\nX_orig_normalized = adata_orig.X.toarray() if sparse.issparse(adata_orig.X) else adata_orig.X\n```\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs without crashing for over 300 seconds\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution\n- The batch integration algorithm is now processing the data correctly\n\n## Algorithm Details\nThe submission implements a \"Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1\" method:\n1. Calculates PC1 of normalized data\n2. Subtracts PC1 component from the data\n3. Runs ComBat on the residuals\n4. Adds PC1 component back\n5. Proceeds with standard SOTA pipeline (PCA + balanced KNN)\n\nThis is an innovative approach to preserve important biological variation while removing batch effects.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The\
    \ debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/logos')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse\nfrom integration_utils import get_stabilized_combat_matrix, build_balanced_knn\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Logos II: Novel Method - Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1\")\n\n    # Step 1: Pre-process and calculate PC1 of the original data\n    adata_orig = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_orig)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_orig)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_orig, n_comps=1, random_state=0)\n\n    pc1_scores = adata_orig.obsm['X_pca']\n    pc1_loadings = adata_orig.varm['PCs']\n\n    # Step 2: Subtract the PC1 component from the normalized data\n    X_orig_normalized = adata_orig.X.toarray() if sparse.issparse(adata_orig.X)\
    \ else adata_orig.X\n    X_residuals = X_orig_normalized - (pc1_scores @ pc1_loadings.T)\n\n    # Step 3: Run ComBat on the residual data\n    adata_residuals = ad.AnnData(X=X_residuals, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n    X_corrected_residuals = get_stabilized_combat_matrix(adata_residuals) # This function expects normalized data\n\n    # Step 4: Add the PC1 component back\n    X_final = X_corrected_residuals + (pc1_scores @ pc1_loadings.T)\n\n    # Step 5: Proceed with the rest of the SOTA pipeline\n    adata_final = ad.AnnData(X=X_final, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_final, n_comps=50, random_state=0)\n\n    Z_emb = adata_final.obsm['X_pca']\n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(Z_emb, adata.obs['batch'].values, n_neighbors_total=42, metric='cosine')\n\n    return ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={'method_id': 'logos_subtract_add_back_pc1_v1', 'neighbors': {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}},\n\
    \        obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb},\n        obsp={'connectivities': C, 'distances': D}\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLogos II: Novel Method - Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/b90bde24-cbef-4edc-af84-c8bfa6e7da9d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: b90bde24-cbef-4edc-af84-c8bfa6e7da9d\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_simple.py:392: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in log1p\n  np.log1p(X, out=X)\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_simple.py:392: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered\
    \ in log1p\n  np.log1p(X, out=X)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Novel Method: Subtract-and-Add-Back PC1' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 272.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat\
    \ Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether\
    \ I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 251 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Auto-τ Whitening + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 150 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 235 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.97) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.075 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 234 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.93) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.078 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 224 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.7) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 131 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.827 | 0.181 | 0.123 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.844 |\n\nPage 1 of 28 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-28,\
