    \  ASW_batch: 0.820451  ASW_label: 0.543821  ARI: 0.620091  NMI: 0.682058\n  Graph_conn: 0.889813  kBET: 0.617160  iLISI: 0.036763  cLISI: 0.996679\n  PCR: 0.690959  Cell_cycle: 0.314662\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Performing Targeted ComBat Correction ---\n  Learning ComBat params on residual data...\n  Applying learned params to original data...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/e31ce9ec-7dcd-4916-8f7b-d2df091b2517/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: e31ce9ec-7dcd-4916-8f7b-d2df091b2517\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be\
    \ tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual\
    \ BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I\
    \ | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 251 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Auto-τ Whitening + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 150 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 235 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.97) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.075 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 234 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.93) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.078 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 224 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.7) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 131 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.827 | 0.181 | 0.123 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.844 |\n\nPage 1 of 28 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-28,\
    \ `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
